'cause you look so fabulous.

00:00:06.765 --> 00:00:09.155
You said, did your brother, was
your brother a part of this?

00:00:09.155 --> 00:00:10.872
- My brother made this.

00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:11.705
Isn't this wonderful?

00:00:11.705 --> 00:00:14.702
(audience cheers)
(Wendy cheers)

00:00:14.702 --> 00:00:15.535
- Yes.
- That's like

00:00:15.535 --> 00:00:17.358
something I would wear on tour
with the see-through aspect,

00:00:17.358 --> 00:00:19.028
the whole catsuit
underneath, it's so cute.

00:00:19.028 --> 00:00:20.214
I love it so much, it's so hot.

00:00:20.214 --> 00:00:21.047
Anyway-
- Thank you!

00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:21.880
- I had to say that.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:22.713
- Oh!
- Have you met Nick before?

00:00:22.713 --> 00:00:24.190
- No, and I'm fanning out.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.517
I'm trying to contain myself,
(audience laughs)

00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:27.513
but no, I love you.

00:00:27.513 --> 00:00:30.053
I love you, I've loved you for
years, you and your brothers.

00:00:30.053 --> 00:00:30.886
(Kelly giggles)
Pleasure.

00:00:30.886 --> 00:00:31.728
- Nice to meet you.
- Pleasure.

00:00:31.728 --> 00:00:32.561
- Alright,

00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:35.129
so you got to play Issa
Rae's mom on Insecure, right?

00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:36.528
- Yes, yes.
- Yeah.

00:00:36.528 --> 00:00:37.687
So that was,

00:00:37.687 --> 00:00:38.632
you have a connection with her

00:00:38.632 --> 00:00:39.765
that I think is really remarkable

00:00:39.765 --> 00:00:41.547
'cause I wanna get to what you do-

00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:42.380
- Wow.
- in a minute as well.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:43.213
So how do you know her?

00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:44.046
Tell everybody.

00:00:44.046 --> 00:00:48.681
- So 26 years ago, I co-founded
Amazing Grace Conservatory.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.661
It's my passion project.

00:00:50.661 --> 00:00:52.328
It's a performing arts school.

00:00:52.328 --> 00:00:53.619
In south LA.
- It's an incredible project.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:54.498
Yeah.
- Thank you.

00:00:54.498 --> 00:00:57.177
And we've had some incredible
alumni to come out,

00:00:57.177 --> 00:00:58.815
and Issa Rae was one of them.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:58.815 --> 00:01:00.294
- Ashton Sanders.

00:01:00.294 --> 00:01:02.013
He's currently in "I
Wanna Dance With Somebody"

00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:03.321
playing Bobby Brown,

00:01:03.321 --> 00:01:05.608
and she was one of my students.

00:01:05.608 --> 00:01:06.441
- Yeah.

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:09.546
- And then to come full circle
and to see what she has done-

00:01:09.546 --> 00:01:10.379
- Yeah.

00:01:10.379 --> 00:01:12.026
- in this industry is just, it's amazing.

00:01:12.026 --> 00:01:14.074
And I played her mom,

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.407
so it was such a incredible
full-circle moment

00:01:16.407 --> 00:01:18.037
'cause I was still in awe of, you know,

00:01:18.037 --> 00:01:20.903
everything that she's been
doing and what she is, you know,

00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:23.725
and she's created a pipeline
for so many young people,

00:01:23.725 --> 00:01:26.516
especially alumni out of
Amazing Grace Conservatory.

00:01:26.516 --> 00:01:28.012
- Because she was taught to do that,

00:01:28.012 --> 00:01:29.062
because that's what you started.

00:01:29.062 --> 00:01:30.445
That domino effect is incredible.

00:01:30.445 --> 00:01:31.278
- It is.
(audience cheers)

00:01:31.278 --> 00:01:33.728
- And I think it's such a
testament to what you're doing

00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:35.359
that people are coming out of it

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:38.513
and having success and feeling
confident and landing jobs.

00:01:38.513 --> 00:01:40.048
Like that's an incredible thing.

00:01:40.048 --> 00:01:40.881
- Thank you.

00:01:40.881 --> 00:01:42.131
- I learned about that and I
was like, I didn't know that.

00:01:42.131 --> 00:01:43.170
That's super cool.
- Wow.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.734
- Yeah.
- And I, you know,

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.912
we started it as two struggling artists.

00:01:46.912 --> 00:01:48.955
You know, my best friend-
- As we all do.

00:01:48.955 --> 00:01:50.196
- Hello, hello!
- Yeah.

00:01:50.196 --> 00:01:51.388
Who hasn't been a waitress?

00:01:51.388 --> 00:01:52.323
(Wendy and Kelly laugh)

00:01:52.323 --> 00:01:53.390
- Well I haven't, thank God,

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:54.738
they don't want me waitin'.
(Kelly screams)

00:01:54.738 --> 00:01:55.571
Girl!
(audience laughs)

00:01:55.571 --> 00:01:56.404
They don't want me waiting tables.

00:01:56.404 --> 00:01:57.237
(Wendy laughs)
- I feel like

00:01:57.237 --> 00:01:58.907
we were all waiters or
waitresses at some point.

00:01:58.907 --> 00:02:01.209
- I tried, I'm a little clumsy.

00:02:01.209 --> 00:02:03.237
- So your show is called "The Game,"

00:02:03.237 --> 00:02:05.462
and it's been on since 2006.

00:02:05.462 --> 00:02:09.739
So, but this is the second
season of the revival, right?

00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:10.851
- It's the second, yeah.

00:02:10.851 --> 00:02:13.003
I wanna call it a "re-imagining."

00:02:13.003 --> 00:02:13.836
- Okay, re-imagining.
- Yeah.

00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:14.669
- Yeah, I like that too.

00:02:14.669 --> 00:02:15.502
- Yes.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:18.252
Not a reboot, but it's a
re-imagining of "The Game."

00:02:18.252 --> 00:02:19.085
Yeah.
- So why

00:02:19.085 --> 00:02:19.918
do you like to call it that instead?

00:02:19.918 --> 00:02:22.876
- Because, you know, it's
familiar, but it's fresh.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:23.709
- Yeah.
- So we kept

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.137
a lot of the same elements,

00:02:25.137 --> 00:02:29.460
but it's, we just upped
the antes of it, you know?

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.577
- Yeah.
- It was originally set

00:02:30.577 --> 00:02:31.700
in San Diego,

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.630
so all the characters
were there in San Diego,

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.879
and now we've moved the show to Vegas.

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:36.712
- Yeah.

00:02:36.712 --> 00:02:37.619
- So it's hot, it's spicy.

00:02:37.619 --> 00:02:38.452
- Very different town.

00:02:38.452 --> 00:02:39.353
- Woo, very different!
- Yeah.

00:02:39.353 --> 00:02:41.497
- You know what happens
in Vegas stays in Vegas.

00:02:41.497 --> 00:02:42.330
- Yeah.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.163
- Unless it's on "The Game."

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:43.996
- Sometimes it follows you home.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:45.506
- Exactly, exactly.

00:02:45.506 --> 00:02:50.371
So we've added some
incredible talent to the cast.

00:02:50.371 --> 00:02:51.204
- Yeah.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.685
- And it's shown through the lens

00:02:52.685 --> 00:02:55.865
of the daughter of one of
the original cast members.

00:02:55.865 --> 00:02:56.771
- Yeah, I love that.

00:02:56.771 --> 00:02:58.604
- Yeah, so it gives a
whole new perspective

00:02:58.604 --> 00:03:00.201
of the show from football.

00:03:00.201 --> 00:03:01.276
It starts about football,

00:03:01.276 --> 00:03:03.975
but it really holds up
a mirror to America.

00:03:03.975 --> 00:03:04.808
- Yeah.
- And everything

00:03:04.808 --> 00:03:05.641
that we're going through,

00:03:05.641 --> 00:03:07.984
and football just happens
to be the platform.

00:03:07.984 --> 00:03:09.808
- I think it's important
too that art does that,

00:03:09.808 --> 00:03:14.284
is that you do talk about
what's going on in the world.

00:03:14.284 --> 00:03:15.830
I think that's where art is helpful.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:16.663
- Right.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.744
- Because you make
something thought-provoking

00:03:18.744 --> 00:03:20.888
that ends up, the progress
happens from that.

00:03:20.888 --> 00:03:21.949
Hopefully that's the goal.

00:03:21.949 --> 00:03:22.782
- Exactly.
- Yeah.

00:03:22.782 --> 00:03:23.615
- Oh, we're in Vegas,

00:03:23.615 --> 00:03:25.624
so maybe we can come to your residency.

00:03:25.624 --> 00:03:26.457
- You should.

00:03:26.457 --> 00:03:27.290
- Yes.
(audience cheers)

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.034
- I'm telling you, that's a good time.

00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:31.280
- Yes, I know that would be a good time.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.113
- A lot of fun.

00:03:32.113 --> 00:03:32.946
- It's a good time.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:33.779
And I will tell you,

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:34.683
the thing I love about your audience too

00:03:34.683 --> 00:03:37.062
'cause I was like, I didn't
really know like what to expect,

00:03:37.062 --> 00:03:39.351
and I was like, "alright, I'm 40,

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:40.360
I'm showing up, I'm doing it."

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.193
(Wendy laughs)

00:03:41.193 --> 00:03:42.336
And I'm like, I just love
the musics, whatever.

00:03:42.336 --> 00:03:45.219
You have such a a broad fan base.

00:03:45.219 --> 00:03:46.052
Every-
- Yes.

00:03:46.052 --> 00:03:48.823
- every culture, every age, every,

00:03:48.823 --> 00:03:49.706
it was really cool.

00:03:49.706 --> 00:03:50.539
I love the show.

00:03:50.539 --> 00:03:51.918
I think that's cool
that music can do that.

00:03:51.918 --> 00:03:52.751
Bring people together-
- Absolutely.

00:03:52.751 --> 00:03:54.416
- that maybe wouldn't be
the best in the same room,

00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:55.567
or art does that in general.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:56.761
- You should definitely come to the show.

